            "review_text": "desiremmwekb10\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam2964 contributions\n0\nChicken ramen\nJan 2019 • Solo\nI ordered a shoyu chicken ramen. The broth was clear, yet still offered a strong flavor. I like the broth. Taste somewhat like the broth of Vietnamese chicke Pho. As for topping, I liked the pork, tender and \"melting in mouth\" kind of thing. I do not like the chicken strip too much coz it was lean chicken breast with little flavor. Well, it was a good ramen overall but the taste of it was not stand out like tonkotsu or miso ramen. In Vietnam, there are many chicken noodles that would give you this similar taste, just as good. So for me, it was just \"another chicken noodle\" shop.\nRead more\nWritten January 31, 2019",
